#subtitle: Changes on how the Peseta is handled.

= Monetary Policy

Monetary Policy allows us to intervine in the valuation of the Peseta, interest rates and foreign exchange controls.

Spain isn't tied to the gold standard, this give us more flexibility to deal with our monetary policy. However, most of our political allies support maintaining a strong currency, just as has been done since the Primo de Rivera dictatorship.


@monetary_menu

Peseta Exchange Status: **[+ peseta_status +]**
Exchange Control: **[? if exchange_control = 1 : Active (State Divisa Monopoly) ?][? if exchange_control = 0 : Inactive (Free Capital Flow) ?]**
Agrarian Exports Level: [+ agricultural_exports +]

- @peseta_orthodox: Maintain an overvalued Peseta and high interest rates (Orthodoxy / Gold Block).
- @peseta_devalue: Devalue the Peseta and cut interest rates (Pro-Export Strategy).
- @toggle_exchange_control: [? if exchange_control = 0 : Implement ?][? if exchange_control = 1 : Lift ?].
- @root: Do not alter monetary settings.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@peseta_orthodox
title: Defend the Peseta's high valuation (Gold Block Alignment).
subtitle: Reassures foreign bankers and restrains inflation, but chokes credit and depresses exports.
choose-if: peseta_status != "orthodox"
unavailable-subtitle: We already have this stance on the Peseta.
on-arrival: peseta_status = "orthodox"; west_relation += 1; inflation -= 0.3; agricultural_exports -= 2; economic_growth -= 0.3; unemployment += 0.4; polarization -= 5;

We align with orthodox international banking circles by maintaining high interest rates and a artificially strong Peseta. While this controls inflation, high credit costs crush local investment and Spanish agricultural exports become more expensive in foreign markets.

@peseta_devalue
title: Devalue the Peseta and slash interest rates.
subtitle: Sparks an export boom for agriculture (oranges, wine, oil) and eases local credit.
choose-if: peseta_status != "devalued"
unavailable-subtitle: We already have this stance on the Peseta.
on-arrival: peseta_status = "devalued"; inflation += 0.4; west_relation -= 1; unemployment -= 0.5; polarization += 5; economic_growth += 0.2 if tariffs <= 0;

By lowering interest rates and letting the Peseta devalue, we provide cheap credit to domestic producers and make Spanish exports irresistible in international markets.

@toggle_exchange_control
title: [? if exchange_control = 0 : Enforce strict Foreign Exchange Controls (Control de Cambios) ?][? if exchange_control = 1 : Abolish Exchange Controls ?]
subtitle: [? if exchange_control = 0 : Monopolizes foreign currency to stop elite capital flight. ?][? if exchange_control = 1 : Restores free capital movements to regain business trust. ?]
on-arrival: exchange_control = 1 if exchange_control == 0; capital_strike_progress -= 2 if exchange_control == 0; polarization += 10 if exchange_control == 0; prr_relation -= 10 if exchange_control == 0; dlr_relation -= 10 if exchange_control == 0; other_right_republicans_relation -= 10 if exchange_control == 0; pce_relation += 10 if exchange_control == 0; exchange_control = 0 if exchange_control == 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if exchange_control == 1; polarization -= 5 if exchange_control == 1; prr_relation += 5 if exchange_control == 1; dlr_relation += 7 if exchange_control == 1; other_right_republicans_relation += 5 if exchange_control == 1; pce_relation -= 10 if exchange_control == 1;

[? if exchange_control = 1 : We establish a state monopoly over foreign currencies and import licenses. Conservative elites can no longer drain their fortunes into French or Swiss accounts, containing capital flight. ?][? if exchange_control = 0 : We lift state restrictions on currency transactions, attempting to restore financial confidence among commercial banks and foreign investors. ?]
